2. Permission to Use

You are granted a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

(a) download and use official BedrockPassport releases on private or public Minecraft servers, including monetized servers;
(b) create reasonable backup copies for your own use;
(c) compile the unmodified source code for private server use, local testing, security review, troubleshooting, and compatibility testing;
(d) modify configuration files, messages, formatting, and other administrator-facing settings for your own server;
(e) inspect the publicly available source code for security review, learning, troubleshooting, and interoperability;
(f) create a repository fork solely for preparing contributions to the official BedrockPassport project; and
(g) submit patches, pull requests, bug fixes, translations, or other contributions to the official BedrockPassport project.

